{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdKqmsXszUF5gcU5QEeVB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014GgZ6mgUScaEEJN7Rjtkyb","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Hunter: C1 Task 1 domain predicate","subagent_type":"tribe:hunter","run_in_background":false,"prompt":"You are a Hunter implementing ONE task under strict TDD. Work ONLY in this worktree:\n`/Users/todd.lam/WORK/_TestScripts/ai-dict/.claude/worktrees/c1-open-on-install`\nBranch: `feature/C1OpenOnInstallLE5` (already checked out). Do NOT switch branches, do NOT touch any other worktree.\n\n# Task C1 / Task 1 — `shouldOpenOnboardingOnInstall` domain predicate\n\nThis is the pure-domain decision function for campaign card C1 (open onboarding on install). Follow\nthe committed plan verbatim for THIS task: `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-16-c1-open-on-install.md`, Task 1.\n\n## Rule walls (non-negotiable)\n- `packages/app/src/domain/**` stays chrome-free: `reason` is typed `string`, NEVER chrome's\n  `OnInstalledReason`. No `@types/chrome` import may enter `packages/app`.\n- TDD: write the failing test FIRST, run it and SEE it fail, then implement, then see it green.\n\n## Steps\n1. **Write failing test** — create `packages/app/test/onboarding-policy.test.ts` EXACTLY as in the\n   plan's Task 1 Step 1 (6 assertions: install/false→true, install/true→false, update/false→false,\n   update/true→false, and chrome_update/false→false + shared_module_update/false→false).\n   Run: `cd packages/app && bunx vitest run test/onboarding-policy.test.ts`\n   Expect: FAILS (module does not resolve). Capture this output.\n\n2. **Implement** — create `packages/app/src/domain/onboarding-policy.ts` EXACTLY as the plan's Task 1\n   Step 2 (the doc comment + `export function shouldOpenOnboardingOnInstall(reason: string, envKeyBaked: boolean): boolean { return reason === 'install' && !envKeyBaked; }`).\n   Add `export * from './domain/onboarding-policy'; // C1` to