kages/extension-chrome && bunx vitest run test/manifest.test.ts` — expect all pass,\n   including the \"declares only storage + sidePanel\" assertion (proves no permission added).\n   Capture output.\n\n4. **Full gate then commit** (foreground, timeout 600000 each):\n   `cd packages/app && bun run typecheck && cd ../extension-chrome && bun run typecheck && cd ../.. && bun run lint && bun run format:check`\n   Paste ALL output verbatim. Then:\n   ```\n   git add packages/extension-chrome/src/sw.ts\n   git commit -m \"feat: open onboarding on install — wire the onInstalled listener in sw.ts (C1)\" -m $'Tribe-Card: c1-open-on-install\\nTribe-Task: 2/3'\n   ```\n\n## Constraints\n- Every Bash call foreground only (`run_in_background` false/omitted), gates get `timeout: 600000`.\n  NEVER background anything.\n- Touch ONLY `packages/extension-chrome/src/sw.ts`. Do NOT touch manifest.json, e2e files, router,\n  wire, or the domain files. Do NOT open a PR or merge.\n- If a gate fails in a way outside this exact scope, STOP and report — do not guess.\n\n## Report\nAppend \"## Hunter — C1 Task 2\" to\n`/Users/todd.lam/WORK/_TestScripts/ai-dict/.claude/state/least-effort-5/reports/C1.md` with: the\ntypecheck output, the manifest.test.ts output, the full gate output, and the commit SHA. Then give\nme a one-paragraph summary.","uuid":"aa746448-a7c9-4b11-be31-148fc63e0d2d","session_id":"1582a562-7cd7-4915-90db-f6e0a641a53f"}
