{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdKrFxCCeuChqcKCn9nTQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XziskdYZBHMSnd1CPfVSAv","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/todd.lam/WORK/_TestScripts/ai-dict/.claude/state/least-effort-5/reports/C1.md","old_string":"- Plan checkboxes were NOT ticked (per brief instruction — Warchief's responsibility).\n- No PR opened, no merge, no `sw.ts` or e2e file touched.","new_string":"- Plan checkboxes were NOT ticked (per brief instruction — Warchief's responsibility).\n- No PR opened, no merge, no `sw.ts` or e2e file touched.\n\n## Hunter — C1 Task 2\n\nTask: wire `chrome.runtime.onInstalled` listener in `sw.ts` (Task 2/3 of\n`docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-16-c1-open-on-install.md`), with the brief's **CRITICAL MECHANISM\nOVERRIDE (campaign ruling R1)**: use `chrome.tabs.create({ url: chrome.runtime.getURL('options.html') })`\ninstead of the plan's `chrome.runtime.openOptionsPage()`.\n\n### Implementation\n\nEdited `packages/extension-chrome/src/sw.ts` only:\n1. Added `shouldOpenOnboardingOnInstall,` to the `@ai-dict/app` import block, right after\n   `configuredProvidersFor,`.\n2. Inserted the new `chrome.runtime.onInstalled.addListener(...)` block immediately after the\n   `chrome.commands.onCommand.addListener(...)` block's closing `});` and before the\n   `// Side panel:` comment, exactly per the brief (using `chrome.tabs.create` +\n   `chrome.runtime.getURL('options.html')`, never `openOptionsPage()` or `chrome.tabs.query`).\n   The pre-existing `chrome.sidePanel?.setPanelBehavior?.(...)` line was left untouched.\n\nNo dedicated unit test exists for `sw.ts` (composition root, covered by e2e only in Task 3 — per\nplan's own framing for this task), so there is no RED/GREEN cycle for this task; correctness is\nproven by the typecheck gate + the manifest regression guard named in the brief.\n\n### Typecheck gate\n\nCommand: `cd packages/extension-chrome && bun run typecheck`\n```\n$ tsc --noEmit\n```\n(clean — no errors)\n\n### Manifest regression guard\n\nCommand: `cd packages/extension-chrome && bunx vitest run test/manifest.test.ts`\n```\n RUN  v4.1.8 /Users/todd.lam/WORK/_TestScripts/ai-dict/.claude/worktrees/c1-open-on-install/packages/extension-chrome\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  6 passed (6)\n   Start at  06:21:21\n   Duration  396ms (transform 21ms, setup 0ms, import 42ms, tests 3ms, environment 244ms)\n```\nAll 6 assertions pass, including the \"declares only storage + sidePanel\" assertion — proves no\nmanifest permission was added by this change.\n\n### Formatting note\n\nThe brief's snippet (`void Promise.resolve(\\n  chrome.tabs.create(...),\\n).catch(...)`) does not\nmatch this repo's Prettier config — `bun run format:check` flagged `sw.ts` on the first pass. Fixed\nby reflowing to Prettier's own preferred wrap (`void Promise.resolve(chrome.tabs.create({ url:\nchrome.runtime.getURL('options.html') })).catch(\\n  () => undefined,\\n);`) — semantically identical\ncode, only line-break placement changed. Re-ran the gate below after the fix; all clean.\n\n### Full gate (verbatim, after the formatting fix)\n\nCommand: `cd packages/app && bun run typecheck && cd ../extension-chrome && bun run typecheck && cd ../.. && bun run lint && bun run format:check`\n```\n$ tsc --noEmit\n$ tsc --noEmit\n$ bun scripts/check-dep-direction.mjs && eslint .\n✓ dependency direction OK — all imports point inward (ref-core-dependency-rule)\n$ prettier --check .\nChecking formatting...\nAll matched files use Prettier code style!\n```\n\nRe-confirmed `test/manifest.test.ts` still green after the formatting fix (same 6/6 pass, rerun\nseparately).\n\n### Commit\n\nDiff scoped to exactly one file:\n```\nM  packages/extension-chrome/src/sw.ts\n```\n(17 insertions, 0 deletions — the import line + the new listener block; the pre-existing\n`chrome.sidePanel?.setPanelBehavior?.(...)` line is unchanged in the diff.)\n\nCommit message:\n```\nfeat: open onboarding on install — wire the onInstalled listener in sw.ts (C1)\n\nTribe-Card: c1-open-on-install\nTribe-Task: 2/3\n```\n\nCommit SHA: `8f09fef`\n\n### Scope check\n\n- Only `packages/extension-chrome/src/sw.ts` touched — no manifest.json, e2e, router, wire, or\n  domain file changes.\n- Decision logic stays in the domain predicate (`shouldOpenOnboardingOnInstall`); `sw.ts` only\n  makes the `chrome.*` calls.\n- Used `chrome.tabs.create` per campaign ruling R1 override, NOT `openOptionsPage()` and NOT\n  `chrome.tabs.query`.\n- `.catch(() => undefined)` idiom matches the existing fire-and-forget style already in the file.\n- Plan checkboxes were NOT ticked (per brief instruction — Warchief's responsibility).\n- No PR opened, no merge, no e2e file touched (Task 3 is a separate task)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2854,"cache_read_input_tokens":44809,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2854,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01KkzquWRyxyPdhi8urnoqHJ","session_id":"1582a562-7cd7-4915-90db-f6e0a641a53f","uuid":"4a54e829-7dc9-4765-80f3-8223dfa5e9a8","timestamp":"2026-07-23T23:23:27.742Z","request_id":"req_011CdKrFwBRw3LscycimvqFk","subagent_type":"tribe:hunter","task_description":"Hunter: C1 Task 2 sw.ts listener"}
