{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KkzquWRyxyPdhi8urnoqHJ","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All clean — no stray untracked/modified files (the report file lives outside this git worktree, in the shared `.claude/state` path, which is not part of this repo's tracked tree per the brief instructions).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented Task 2/3 of the C1 plan by editing only `packages/extension-chrome/src/sw.ts`: added `shouldOpenOnboardingOnInstall` to the `@ai-dict/app` import block, then inserted a `chrome.runtime.onInstalled` listener (between the existing `chrome.commands.onCommand` block and the `chrome.sidePanel` startup line) that calls the domain predicate and, per the binding campaign ruling R1 override, opens the welcome screen with `chrome.tabs.create({ url: chrome.runtime.getURL('options.html') })` instead of the plan's original `openOptionsPage()`. `bun run typecheck` was clean in both `packages/app` and `packages/extension-chrome`; `test/manifest.test.ts` passed all 6 assertions (confirming no manifest permission was added); the brief's snippet needed a Prettier reflow (semantically identical, just line-wrap) to satisfy `bun run format:check`, after which the full gate (`typecheck` ×2, `lint`, `format:check`) was clean. Committed as `8f09fef` with the exact commit message and `Tribe-Card`/`Tribe-Task: 2/3` trailers the brief specified, touching only `sw.ts` (17 insertions). Full command output and diff detail are appended to `/Users/todd.lam/WORK/_TestScripts/ai-dict/.claude/state/least-effort-5/reports/C1.md` under \"## Hunter — C1 Task 2\".\n\n- **Status:** DONE\n- **Commit hash:** `8f09fef`\n- **One-line test summary:** manifest.test.ts 6 passed; typecheck/lint/format all clean\n- **Concerns:** None — the only deviation from the brief's literal snippet was a Prettier line-wrap fix (documented in the report and visible in the committed diff), required because the repo's `format:check` gate rejected the brief's exact formatting."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: ac9be2e6c9371c7b2 (use SendMessage with to: 'ac9be2e6c9371c7b2', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent)\n<usage>subagent_tokens: 50793\ntool_uses: 18\nduration_ms: 166798</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1582a562-7cd7-4915-90db-f6e0a641a53f","uuid":"83304680-f8af-4531-aee7-c86a025069a2","timestamp":"2026-07-23T23:23:40.643Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are a Hunter implementing ONE task. Work ONLY in this worktree:\n`/Users/todd.lam/WORK/_TestScripts/ai-dict/.claude/worktrees/c1-open-on-install`\nBranch: `feature/C1OpenOnInstallLE5` (already checked out). `node_modules` is already installed.\nDo NOT switch branches or touch any other worktree.\n\n# Task C1 / Task 2 — wire the `chrome.runtime.onInstalled` listener in `sw.ts`\n\nReference plan: `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-16-c1-open-on-install.md` Task 2. BUT one detail of\nthe plan is SUPERSEDED by a committed campaign ruling — read carefully.\n\n## CRITICAL MECHANISM OVERRIDE (campaign ruling R1 — binding, supersedes plan §2.1 / Task 2 snippet)\nThe plan shows the listener calling `chrome.runtime.openOptionsPage()`. **Do NOT use that.** A\npaid-for debugging finding (ruling R1) established that `openOptionsPage()` called synchronously\nfrom `onInstalled` at cold `--load-extension` launch resolves with NO error but creates NO tab.\nUse `chrome.tabs.create` instead:\n\n```ts\nvoid Promise.resolve(\n  chrome.tabs.create({ url: chrome.runtime.getURL('options.html') }),\n).catch(() => undefined);\n```\n\n`chrome.tabs.create` and `chrome.runtime.getURL` require NO manifest permission (the `tabs`\npermission only governs reading tab URLs/titles, which this does not do), so the manifest stays\n`[\"storage\",\"sidePanel\"]` and `manifest.test.ts` stays green untouched. Do NOT use\n`chrome.tabs.query` (that WOULD need the `tabs` permission — forbidden).\n\n## Rule walls (non-negotiable)\n- The decision stays in the domain predicate; `sw.ts` only does the `chrome.*` calls. Do NOT\n  reimplement the reason/env-key logic inline — call `shouldOpenOnboardingOnInstall`.\n- No manifest change, no wire message, no router change. This is a bare `chrome.*` listener like the\n  existing `chrome.commands.onCommand` one.\n- `.catch(() => undefined)` matches the file's fire-and-forget idiom (see sw.ts:195, sw.ts:199).\n\n## Steps\n1. **Edit `packages/extension-chrome/src/sw.ts`:**\n   a. Add `shouldOpenOnboardingOnInstall,` to the `@ai-dict/app` import block (top of file), on its\n      own line right after `configuredProvidersFor,` (currently line 4).\n   b. Insert this block immediately AFTER the `chrome.commands.onCommand.addListener(...)` block's\n      closing `});` (currently line 196) and BEFORE the `// Side panel:` comment / `chrome.sidePanel?.setPanelBehavior` line (currently 198–199):\n\n```ts\n\n// C1: the very first thing a fresh install sees is the welcome screen, instead of the lucky few\n// who stumble into it via the no-key card's \"Open Settings\" button or the side panel. Fires only\n// on a genuine 'install' (never 'update') and is skipped when the build baked a Gemini key\n// (shouldOpenOnboardingOnInstall's own doc comment). Chrome fires onInstalled exactly once per\n// real install, so the reason check alone is the whole \"no re-prompting loop\" guarantee — no\n// extra storage flag needed. Uses chrome.tabs.create (not openOptionsPage) because\n// openOptionsPage() at cold install launch resolves without creating a tab (campaign ruling R1);\n// chrome.tabs.create needs no manifest permission.\nchrome.runtime.onInstalled.addListener((details) => {\n  if (shouldOpenOnboardingOnInstall(details.reason, Boolean(ENV_API_KEY))) {\n    void Promise.resolve(\n      chrome.tabs.create({ url: chrome.runtime.getURL('options.html') }),\n    ).catch(() => undefined);\n  }\n});\n```\n   Leave the existing `chrome.sidePanel?.setPanelBehavior?.(...)` line exactly as-is (do not modify it).\n\n2. **Typecheck gate** (foreground, timeout 600000):\n   `cd packages/extension-chrome && bun run typecheck` — expect clean. Capture output.\n\n3. **Manifest regression guard** (foreground, timeout 600000):\n   `cd packages/extension-chrome && bunx vitest run test/manifest.test.ts` — expect all pass,\n   including the \"declares only storage + sidePanel\" assertion (proves no permission added).\n   Capture output.\n\n4. **Full gate then commit** (foreground, timeout 600000 each):\n   `cd packages/app && bun run typecheck && cd ../extension-chrome && bun run typecheck && cd ../.. && bun run lint && bun run format:check`\n   Paste ALL output verbatim. Then:\n   ```\n   git add packages/extension-chrome/src/sw.ts\n   git commit -m \"feat: open onboarding on install — wire the onInstalled listener in sw.ts (C1)\" -m $'Tribe-Card: c1-open-on-install\\nTribe-Task: 2/3'\n   ```\n\n## Constraints\n- Every Bash call foreground only (`run_in_background` false/omitted), gates get `timeout: 600000`.\n  NEVER background anything.\n- Touch ONLY `packages/extension-chrome/src/sw.ts`. Do NOT touch manifest.json, e2e files, router,\n  wire, or the domain files. Do NOT open a PR or merge.\n- If a gate fails in a way outside this exact scope, STOP and report — do not guess.\n\n## Report\nAppend \"## Hunter — C1 Task 2\" to\n`/Users/todd.lam/WORK/_TestScripts/ai-dict/.claude/state/least-effort-5/reports/C1.md` with: the\ntypecheck output, the manifest.test.ts output, the full gate output, and the commit SHA. Then give\nme a one-paragraph summary.","agentId":"ac9be2e6c9371c7b2","agentType":"tribe:hunter","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All clean — no stray untracked/modified files (the report file lives outside this git worktree, in the shared `.claude/state` path, which is not part of this repo's tracked tree per the brief instructions).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented Task 2/3 of the C1 plan by editing only `packages/extension-chrome/src/sw.ts`: added `shouldOpenOnboardingOnInstall` to the `@ai-dict/app` import block, then inserted a `chrome.runtime.onInstalled` listener (between the existing `chrome.commands.onCommand` block and the `chrome.sidePanel` startup line) that calls the domain predicate and, per the binding campaign ruling R1 override, opens the welcome screen with `chrome.tabs.create({ url: chrome.runtime.getURL('options.html') })` instead of the plan's original `openOptionsPage()`. `bun run typecheck` was clean in both `packages/app` and `packages/extension-chrome`; `test/manifest.test.ts` passed all 6 assertions (confirming no manifest permission was added); the brief's snippet needed a Prettier reflow (semantically identical, just line-wrap) to satisfy `bun run format:check`, after which the full gate (`typecheck` ×2, `lint`, `format:check`) was clean. Committed as `8f09fef` with the exact commit message and `Tribe-Card`/`Tribe-Task: 2/3` trailers the brief specified, touching only `sw.ts` (17 insertions). Full command output and diff detail are appended to `/Users/todd.lam/WORK/_TestScripts/ai-dict/.claude/state/least-effort-5/reports/C1.md` under \"## Hunter — C1 Task 2\".\n\n- **Status:** DONE\n- **Commit hash:** `8f09fef`\n- **One-line test summary:** manifest.test.ts 6 passed; typecheck/lint/format all clean\n- **Concerns:** None — the only deviation from the brief's literal snippet was a Prettier line-wrap fix (documented in the report and visible in the committed diff), required because the repo's `format:check` gate rejected the brief's exact formatting."}],"resolvedModel":"claude-sonnet-5","totalDurationMs":166798,"totalTokens":50793,"totalToolUseCount":18,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":243,"cache_read_input_tokens":49821,"output_tokens":727,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":243},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2