new c1 spec (verbatim)\n`packages/extension-chrome/e2e/c1-open-on-install.spec.ts`:\n```ts\nimport { test, expect } from './fixtures';\n\n// C1: fresh installs open the welcome screen automatically. The `context` fixture itself IS a\n// simulated fresh install (chromium.launchPersistentContext('', ...) uses a new temp profile per\n// test — see fixtures.ts), so chrome.runtime.onInstalled({ reason: 'install' }) fires and the\n// sw.ts listener opens options.html via chrome.tabs.create (campaign ruling R1). No click or\n// navigation is needed to observe it.\ntest.describe('C1 open onboarding on install', () => {\n  test('a fresh install opens exactly one options.html tab showing the welcome screen', async ({\n    context,\n  }) => {\n    // The install-opened tab may still be materialising when the body starts; poll until it has\n    // appeared, then assert there is exactly one (proves \"opens exactly one tab, once\").\n    await expect\n      .poll(() => context.pages().filter((p) => p.url().includes('options.html')).length, {\n        timeout: 10_000,\n      })\n      .toBe(1);\n\n    const [page] = context.pages().filter((p) => p.url().includes('options.html'));\n    await page!.waitForSelector('onboarding-view');\n    await expect(page!.locator('onboarding-view #key')).toBeVisible();\n  });\n});\n```\n\n## Step 2 — add the identical arrange-fix to all four breaking tests\nIn EACH of these four tests, insert this block on the line IMMEDIATELY BEFORE its existing\n`const optionsPagePromise = context.waitForEvent('page');` line (do not change anything else in\nthose tests):\n```ts\n  // C1 (ruling R3): the fresh-install options tab (onInstalled → chrome.tabs.create) is still open;\n  // openOptionsPage() would focus/reuse it instead of firing a 'page' event. Close any open options\n  // tab first so this test still proves the CTA/gear *creates* the options page (keeps the\n  // waitForEvent('page') assertion falsifiable).\n  for (const p of context.pages()) {\n    if (p.url().includes('options.html')) await p.close();\n  }\n```\nThe four locations: `onboarding.spec.ts` (~line 64), `settings-nav.spec.ts` (~lines 55 AND 69),\n`side-panel.spec.ts` (~line 73). All four tests already destructure `context`. Match each file's\nexisting indentation (2 spaces).\n\n## Step 3 — run the affected specs GREEN (dist is already current; no rebuild needed)\nForeground, timeout 600000:\n```\ncd packages/extension-chrome && bunx playwright test c1-open-on-install.spec.ts onboarding.spec.ts settings-nav.spec.ts side-panel.spec.ts --reporter=list\n```\nExpect: ALL pass (the 1 new c1 test + onboarding's 3 + settings-nav's 3 + side-panel's tests).\nPaste the full summary. If the new c1 test fails because NO options.html tab was created at install\n(rather than a reuse issue), STOP and report — that would mean R1's chrome.tabs.create also yields\nno tab, which is a Warchief decision (bounded retry), not yours.\n\n## Step 4 — R3 falsifiability proof (MANDATORY): break the CTA, show RED, restore, show GREEN\nThis proves the arrange-fix did NOT make the assertion tautological.\n1. Edit `packages/extension-chrome/src/sw.ts`: change the line\n   `  openOptions: () => chrome.runtime.openOptionsPage(),` (currently line 113) to\n   `  openOptions: () => undefined,`  ← temporary break, do NOT commit this.\n2. Rebuild (foreground, timeout 600000): `cd <worktree root> && env -u GEMINI_API_KEY bun run build:chrome`\n3. Run (foreground, timeout 600000): `cd packages/extension-chrome && bunx playwright test onboarding.spec.ts --reporter=list`\n   Expect: the test 'no-key card shows the setup invite and \"Open Settings\" opens the options page'\n   FAILS (waitForEvent('page') timeout). Capture this RED output — this is the proof.\n4. Restore EXACTLY via git: `cd <worktree root> && git checkout -- packages/extension-chrome/src/sw.ts`\n   Confirm `git status` shows sw.ts unmodified.\n5. Rebuild: `env -u GEMINI_API_KEY bun run build:chrome`\n6. Re-run: `cd packages/e