{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q5pe4nFh7XK5M1zB7qQsfR","type":"tool_result","content":"---\n1:# Campaign rulings — \"least-effort-5\" (C1 · C2 · C5 · C7 · C8)\n22:the 2026-07-17 campaign (`feature/C1OpenOnInstall`, `feature/C2VerifiedActivation`,\n29:   - This **supersedes** the \"Resume mechanics for C1\" paragraph in the old R1, which told the\n30:     executor to adopt `feature/C1OpenOnInstall`. That instruction is void.\n39:## R1 · 2026-07-17 · C1 · The `onInstalled` → options-tab mechanism (carried forward)\n51:from the category's own proof gate (C10, already shipped, exists to be that gate).\n73:C1's \"deliberately minimal\" framing forbids adding _features_; it does not forbid making the one\n95:   C10's shipped guard and it supersedes any plan text still saying\n106:## R3 · 2026-07-17 · C1 · The `onboarding.spec.ts` regression R1's fix exposes (carried forward)\n124:  callback, changing behavior for every caller — a far wider blast radius than C1's fence.\n147:C1. The router's `openOptions` callback and R1's `sw.ts` swap are **NOT** to be changed.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0142jVqWPY6uuwNNPKkrHQbw","session_id":"1582a562-7cd7-4915-90db-f6e0a641a53f","uuid":"f883e913-638f-4009-bb2d-b135831df432","timestamp":"2026-07-23T23:38:14.675Z","subagent_type":"tribe:hunter","task_description":"Hunter: C1 Task 3 e2e specs"}
