pec.ts` — test `'with no key, the panel shows the setup invite and Open Settings\n  opens the options page'`.\n\nNo other line in any of the four tests was changed. Indentation matched each file's existing\n2-space style.\n\n### Step 3 — all four affected specs GREEN (verbatim)\n\nCommand: `cd packages/extension-chrome && bunx playwright test c1-open-on-install.spec.ts onboarding.spec.ts settings-nav.spec.ts side-panel.spec.ts --reporter=list`\n\n```\nRunning 14 tests using 1 worker\n\n  ✓   1 e2e/c1-open-on-install.spec.ts:9:3 › C1 open onboarding on install › a fresh install opens exactly one options.html tab showing the welcome screen (1.9s)\n  ✓   2 e2e/onboarding.spec.ts:7:1 › onboarding: activating with a key swaps to the settings screen and persists it (1.2s)\n  ✓   3 e2e/onboarding.spec.ts:33:1 › onboarding: empty key shows an error and never leaves the onboarding screen (1.2s)\n  ✓   4 e2e/onboarding.spec.ts:45:1 › no-key card shows the setup invite and \"Open Settings\" opens the options page (2.8s)\n  ✓   5 e2e/settings-nav.spec.ts:14:1 › no-key setup invite stays centered on a page with a hostile CSS reset (2.4s)\n  ✓   6 e2e/settings-nav.spec.ts:42:1 › card header Settings gear opens the options page (2.5s)\n  ✓   7 e2e/settings-nav.spec.ts:70:1 › side panel header Settings gear opens the options page (1.3s)\n  ✓   8 e2e/side-panel.spec.ts:47:1 › opens on a teaching empty state (key set), not a fake loading spinner (1.3s)\n  ✓   9 e2e/side-panel.spec.ts:61:1 › with no key, the panel shows the setup invite and Open Settings opens the options page (1.2s)\n  ✓  10 e2e/side-panel.spec.ts:88:1 › renders a result delivered via runtime message (1.3s)\n  ✓  11 e2e/side-panel.spec.ts:102:1 › renders the loading state (1.3s)\n  ✓  12 e2e/side-panel.spec.ts:108:1 › renders an error state (1.3s)\n  ✓  13 e2e/side-panel.spec.ts:127:1 › ignores a malformed result payload (guard) and keeps prior content (1.7s)\n  ✓  14 e2e/side-panel.spec.ts:149:1 › lists stored history under Recent and revisits a lookup on click (1.3s)\n\n  14 passed (23.4s)\n```\n\nThe new c1 test opened exactly one `options.html` tab at fresh install (R1's `chrome.tabs.create`\nfired and materialised the tab) — no STOP condition (Step 3's \"no tab created\" escalation clause)\nwas triggered.\n\n### Step 4 — R3 falsifiability proof (mandatory)\n\n1. Broke the CTA path: edited `packages/extension-chrome/src/sw.ts` line 113 from\n   `openOptions: () => chrome.runtime.openOptionsPage(),` to `openOptions: () => undefined,`\n   (temporary, NOT committed).\n2. Rebuilt: `env -u GEMINI_API_KEY bun run build:chrome` — succeeded (`dist/sw.js 447.4kb` etc.).\n3. Ran `cd packages/extension-chrome && bunx playwright test onboarding.spec.ts --reporter=list` —\n   RED, verbatim:\n\n```\nRunning 3 tests using 1 worker\n\n  ✓  1 e2e/onboarding.spec.ts:7:1 › onboarding: activating with a key swaps to the settings screen and persists it (1.9s)\n  ✓  2 e2e/onboarding.spec.ts:33:1 › onboarding: empty key shows an error and never leaves the onboarding screen (1.3s)\n  ✘  3 e2e/onboarding.spec.ts:45:1 › no-key card shows the setup invite and \"Open Settings\" opens the options page (1.0m)\n\n  1) e2e/onboarding.spec.ts:45:1 › no-key card shows the setup invite and \"Open Settings\" opens the options page\n\n    Test timeout of 60000ms exceeded.\n\n    Error: browserContext.waitForEvent: Target page, context or browser has been closed\n\n      69 |     if (p.url().includes('options.html')) await p.close();\n      70 |   }\n    > 71 |   const optionsPagePromise = context.waitForEvent('page');\n         |                                      ^\n      72 |   await card.locator('.setup-cta').click();\n      73 |   const optionsPage = await optionsPagePromise;\n      74 |   await optionsPage.waitForLoadState();\n        at .../packages/extension-chrome/e2e/onboarding.spec.ts:71:38\n\n  1 failed\n    e2e/onboarding.spec.ts:45:1 › no-key card shows the setup invite and \"Open Settings\" ope