hief. Your job is to execute it exactly.\n\n## Files\n- CREATE `packages/extension-chrome/e2e/c1-open-on-install.spec.ts`\n- MODIFY `packages/extension-chrome/e2e/onboarding.spec.ts` (the test at line 45)\n- MODIFY `packages/extension-chrome/e2e/settings-nav.spec.ts` (the tests at lines 42 and 63)\n- MODIFY `packages/extension-chrome/e2e/side-panel.spec.ts` (the test at line 61)\n\n## Step 1 — create the new c1 spec (verbatim)\n`packages/extension-chrome/e2e/c1-open-on-install.spec.ts`:\n```ts\nimport { test, expect } from './fixtures';\n\n// C1: fresh installs open the welcome screen automatically. The `context` fixture itself IS a\n// simulated fresh install (chromium.launchPersistentContext('', ...) uses a new temp profile per\n// test — see fixtures.ts), so chrome.runtime.onInstalled({ reason: 'install' }) fires and the\n// sw.ts listener opens options.html via chrome.tabs.create (campaign ruling R1). No click or\n// navigation is needed to observe it.\ntest.describe('C1 open onboarding on install', () => {\n  test('a fresh install opens exactly one options.html tab showing the welcome screen', async ({\n    context,\n  }) => {\n    // The install-opened tab may still be materialising when the body starts; poll until it has\n    // appeared, then assert there is exactly one (proves \"opens exactly one tab, once\").\n    await expect\n      .poll(() => context.pages().filter((p) => p.url().includes('options.html')).length, {\n        timeout: 10_000,\n      })\n      .toBe(1);\n\n    const [page] = context.pages().filter((p) => p.url().includes('options.html'));\n    await page!.waitForSelector('onboarding-view');\n    await expect(page!.locator('onboarding-view #key')).toBeVisible();\n  });\n});\n```\n\n## Step 2 — add the identical arrange-fix to all four breaking tests\nIn EACH of these four tests, insert this block on the line IMMEDIATELY BEFORE its existing\n`const optionsPagePromise = context.waitForEvent('page');` line (do not change anything else in\nthose tests):\n```ts\n  // C1 (ruling R3): the fresh-install options tab (onInstalled → chrome.tabs.create) is still open;\n  // openOptionsPage() would focus/reuse it instead of firing a 'page' event. Close any open options\n  // tab first so this test still proves the CTA/gear *creates* the options page (keeps the\n  // waitForEvent('page') assertion falsifiable).\n  for (const p of context.pages()) {\n    if (p.url().includes('options.html')) await p.close();\n  }\n```\nThe four locations: `onboarding.spec.ts` (~line 64), `settings-nav.spec.ts` (~lines 55 AND 69),\n`side-panel.spec.ts` (~line 73). All four tests already destructure `context`. Match each file's\nexisting indentation (2 spaces).\n\n## Step 3 — run the affected specs GREEN (dist is already current; no rebuild needed)\nForeground, timeout 600000:\n```\ncd packages/extension-chrome && bunx playwright test c1-open-on-install.spec.ts onboarding.spec.ts settings-nav.spec.ts side-panel.spec.ts --reporter=list\n```\nExpect: ALL pass (the 1 new c1 test + onboarding's 3 + settings-nav's 3 + side-panel's tests).\nPaste the full summary. If the new c1 test fails because NO options.html tab was created at install\n(rather than a reuse issue), STOP and report — that would mean R1's chrome.tabs.create also yields\nno tab, which is a Warchief decision (bounded retry), not yours.\n\n## Step 4 — R3 falsifiability proof (MANDATORY): break the CTA, show RED, restore, show GREEN\nThis proves the arrange-fix did NOT make the assertion tautological.\n1. Edit `packages/extension-chrome/src/sw.ts`: change the line\n   `  openOptions: () => chrome.runtime.openOptionsPage(),` (currently line 113) to\n   `  openOptions: () => undefined,`  ← temporary break, do NOT commit this.\n2. Rebuild (foreground, timeout 600000): `cd <worktree root> && env -u GEMINI_API_KEY bun run build:chrome`\n3. Run (foreground, timeout 600000): `cd packages/extension-chrome && bunx playwright test onboarding.spec.ts --reporter=list`\n   Expect: the test 'no-key card shows the setup invite and \"Open Settings\" opens the options page'\n   FAILS (waitForEvent('page') timeout). Capture this RED output — this is the proof.\n4. Restore EXACTLY via git: `cd <worktree root> && git checkout -- packages/extension-chrome/src/sw.ts`\n   Confirm `git status` shows sw.ts unmodified.\n5. Rebuild: `env -u GEMINI_API_KEY bun run build:chrome`\n6. Re-run: `cd packages/extension-chrome && bunx playwright test onboarding.spec.ts --reporter=list`\n   Expect: all onboarding tests GREEN. Capture this output.\n\n## Step 5 — gate + commit (only the four e2e files)\nForeground, timeout 600000:\n```\ncd <worktree root> && bun run lint && bun run format:check\n```\nPaste output. Then commit ONLY the four e2e files (NOT sw.ts — it must be unmodified vs HEAD):\n```\ngit add packages/extension-chrome/e2e/c1-open-on-install.spec.ts packages/extension-chrome/e2e/onboarding.spec.ts packages/extension-chrome/e2e/settings-nav.spec.ts packages/extension-chrome/e2e/side-panel.spec.ts\ngit commit -m \"feat: open onboarding on install — add e2e coverage for the onInstalled flow (C1)\" -m $'Tribe-Card: c1-open-on-install\\nTribe-Task: 3/3'\n```\nBefore committing, run `git status` and confirm sw.ts is NOT staged/modified.\n\n## Constraints\n- Every Bash call foreground only (`run_in_background` false/omitted); gates/builds/e2e get\n  `timeout: 600000`. NEVER background anything. A ~4–5 min foreground e2e run is normal.\n- Every build uses `env -u GEMINI_API_KEY bun run build:chrome` (this shell exports GEMINI_API_KEY;\n  leaving it set bakes an env key and disables onboarding → all onboarding e2e fails deterministically).\n- Do NOT commit any sw.ts change. Do NOT touch the domain files, manifest, router, or any spec other\n  than the four named.\n\n## Report\nAppend \"## Hunter — C1 Task 3\" to\n`/Users/todd.lam/WORK/_TestScripts/ai-dict/.claude/state/least-effort-5/reports/C1.md` with: the\nStep 3 all-green output, the Step 4 RED output AND the restored GREEN output, the lint/format output,\n`git status` confirming sw.ts clean, and the commit SHA. Then give me a one-paragraph summary.","agentId":"aa130afecdc75cae8","agentType":"tribe:hunter","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All work is complete: the new e2e spec was created, the identical arrange-fix was applied to the four regression-exposed tests, all 14 tests pass, the R3 falsifiability proof went RED then GREEN as expected, gates are clean, and the commit lands with only the four e2e files (sw.ts and the plan file both verified untouched vs HEAD).\n\n**Status:** DONE\n\n**Commit hash:** `913f32281075e50d19c0d2b66958bcc296e44337`\n\n**One-line test summary:** 14 passed (c1-open-on-install.spec.ts ×1, onboarding.spec.ts ×3, settings-nav.spec.ts ×3, side-panel.spec.ts ×7); R3 falsifiability proof correctly went RED (1 failed, timeout) with the CTA broken, then GREEN (3 passed) after restore.\n\n**Concerns:** I found the plan file with Task 3's checkboxes (`docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-16-c1-open-on-install.md`) but did not tick them or include the file in the commit — the brief's exact `git add`/commit instructions list only the four e2e files (\"commit ONLY the four e2e files\"), and I confirmed via `git log` that Tasks 1 and 2's commits for this same card (`2dbf77d`, `8f09fef`) followed the identical pattern, each hunter noting the checkboxes were deliberately left untouched per brief instruction. This technically deviates from my system prompt's general Method step 7, but matches explicit brief scope and established campaign precedent. Flagged in the report file for the Warchief to tick in a fast docs-only follow-up if desired.\n\nRelevant paths:\n- `/Users/todd.lam/WORK/_TestScripts/ai-dict/.claude/worktrees/c1-open-on-install/packages/extension-chrome/e2e/c1-open-on-install.spec.ts` (new)\n- `/Users/todd.lam/WORK/_TestScripts/ai-dict/.claude/worktrees/c1-open-on-install/packages/extension-chrome/e2e/onboarding.spec.ts`\n- `/Users/todd.lam/WORK/_TestScrip