{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdKtvGpRRCpmxXm81XNYz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`a4-evidence` and `keyboard-commands` both drive the lookup on a `page` variable. I have precise targets. Dispatching a Hunter to apply the `bringToFront` fix to all `relayCommand` call sites and prove determinism with repeat runs."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6039,"cache_read_input_tokens":149753,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6039},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1582a562-7cd7-4915-90db-f6e0a641a53f","uuid":"52042b39-0c8c-4ddd-b467-b917b4f6f54c","timestamp":"2026-07-23T23:58:53.793Z","request_id":"req_011CdKtvEhg8pdqEEwLvLdSj"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdKtvGpRRCpmxXm81XNYz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TrusQ4SPAy3jeMtZnuhBB5","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Hunter: fix relayCommand e2e race","subagent_type":"tribe:hunter","run_in_background":false,"prompt":"You are a Hunter applying ONE targeted fix. Work ONLY in this worktree:\n`/Users/todd.lam/WORK/_TestScripts/ai-dict/.claude/worktrees/c1-open-on-install`\nBranch: `feature/C1OpenOnInstallLE5` (checked out). `node_modules` installed. Do NOT switch branches\nor touch other worktrees.\n\n# Fix: keep command-relay e2e deterministic under C1's install tab\n\nContext (already decided by the Warchief — do NOT re-litigate): C1 makes a fresh install open an\n`options.html` tab via `chrome.runtime.onInstalled` → `chrome.tabs.create`. The e2e fixture launches\na fresh profile per test, so that install tab now lingers in every test. The `relayCommand` helper\n(`e2e/helpers.ts`) relays a command to `chrome.tabs.query({ active: true, lastFocusedWindow: true })`\n— mirroring production's SW onCommand relay. With the install tab present, the *install* tab can be\nthe active tab, so the command lands on `options.html` (no lookup content script) instead of the\npage the test is driving. This is a timing race → tests using `relayCommand` are now flaky/failing.\n\nThe Warchief has verified the fix: calling `await <pageUnderTest>.bringToFront()` immediately before\nthe relay deterministically makes the intended page the active/last-focused tab, so the command\nreaches it. This is a test-arrange fix only — NO product/source change, assertions unchanged (still\nfully falsifiable). It applies R3's standing principle (pre-existing e2e tests adapt in-arrange to\nC1's install tab; the product is untouched).\n\n## Scope — exactly these three specs, all `relayCommand` consumers\n- `packages/extension-chrome/e2e/keyboard-commands.spec.ts`\n- `packages/extension-chrome/e2e/lookup-pending-dismiss.spec.ts`\n- `packages/extension-chrome/e2e/a4-evidence.spec.ts`\n\n## The edit rule (apply to EVERY test that calls `relayCommand`)\nIn each test, add exactly this line immediately BEFORE the FIRST `await relayCommand(sw, ...)` call\nin that test:\n```ts\n  await page.bringToFront(); // C1: make the page under test the active tab so the command relay targets it, not the install-opened options tab (ruling R3)\n```\nIn ALL these tests the page the test drives is the variable named `page` (the one passed to\n`selectWord`/`gotoFixture`/`openTrigger`). Match each file's existing indentation. One\n`bringToFront()` before the first relay per test is enough — the page stays frontmost for any\nlater relays in the same test (no new tab is activated between them). Call sites for reference:\n- keyboard-commands.spec.ts: relays at ~lines 27, 45, 65, 84, 103, 134 (six separate tests → six\n  inserts, each before that test's first relay).\n- lookup-pending-dismiss.spec.ts: relay at ~line 35 (one insert).\n- a4-evidence.spec.ts: relays at ~lines 90 and 95 in ONE test → a single insert before line 90.\n\nDo NOT touch helpers.ts, sw.ts, any domain/source file, or any other spec.\n\n## Verify (foreground, timeout 600000 on each)\n1. Build CI-style (this shell exports GEMINI_API_KEY — clear it; add dummy GA4 creds like CI does so\n   the telemetry-dependent specs behave as in CI):\n   ```\n   cd <worktree root> && env -u GEMINI_API_KEY GA4_MEASUREMENT_ID=G-E2ETEST GA4_API_SECRET=e2e-secret bun run build:chrome\n   ```\n2. Run the three specs with repeat to prove the race is gone:\n   ```\n   cd packages/extension-chrome && bunx playwright test keyboard-commands.spec.ts lookup-pending-dismiss.spec.ts a4-evidence.spec.ts --repeat-each=3 --reporter=list\n   ```\n   Expect: ALL green across all 3 repeats (0 failed). Paste the summary. If ANY test still fails or\n   flakes, STOP and report the exact failure — do not iterate blindly.\n\n## Gate + commit (foreground, timeout 600000)\n```\ncd <worktree root> && bun run lint && bun run format:check\n```\nPaste output. Then commit ONLY the three spec files:\n```\ngit add packages/extension-chrome/e2e/keyboard-commands.spec.ts packages/extension-chrome/e2e/lookup-pending-dismiss.spec.ts packages/extension-chrome/e2e/a4-evidence.spec.ts\ngit commit -m \"test: open onboarding on install — target the page under test in command-relay e2e so the install tab does not steal the command (C1)\" -m $'Tribe-Card: c1-open-on-install\\nTribe-Task: 3b/3'\n```\nRun `git status` before committing and confirm ONLY those three files are staged and sw.ts/domain\nfiles are untouched.\n\n## Constraints\n- Every Bash call foreground only (`run_in_background` false/omitted); builds/e2e get\n  `timeout: 600000`. NEVER background anything.\n- If the repeat run shows residual flakiness, STOP and report — do not guess further fixes.\n\n## Report\nAppend \"## Hunter — C1 Fix 3b (command-relay determinism)\" to\n`/Users/todd.lam/WORK/_TestScripts/ai-dict/.claude/state/least-effort-5/reports/C1.md` with: the\n--repeat-each=3 all-green summary, the lint/format output, `git status` confirmation, and the commit\nSHA. Then give me a one-paragraph summary."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6039,"cache_read_input_tokens":149753,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6039},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1582a562-7cd7-4915-90db-f6e0a641a53f","uuid":"dc022f88-4ce1-42d9-9cc9-f416bf8d9771","timestamp":"2026-07-23T23:58:53.795Z","request_id":"req_011CdKtvEhg8pdqEEwLvLdSj"}
