kages/extension-chrome && bunx playwright test keyboard-commands.spec.ts \\\n  lookup-pending-dismiss.spec.ts a4-evidence.spec.ts --repeat-each=3 --reporter=list\n```\nResult:\n```\nRunning 24 tests using 1 worker\n...\n  3 skipped\n  21 passed (1.0m)\n```\nAll 21 applicable test instances (7 tests x 3 repeats = 21, across keyboard-commands.spec.ts\n[6 tests] and lookup-pending-dismiss.spec.ts [1 test]) passed on every repeat — 0 failed, 0\nflaked. The 3 skips are all `a4-evidence.spec.ts`'s single test, which is gated by\n`test.skip(!RUN, ...)` behind `PLAYWRIGHT_RUN_EVIDENCE=1` (an intentional, pre-existing gate\nunrelated to this fix — it is not part of the normal suite and was correctly skipped both before\nand after this change).\n\n### Gates\n\n```\n$ bun run lint\n$ bun scripts/check-dep-direction.mjs && eslint .\n✓ dependency direction OK — all imports point inward (ref-core-dependency-rule)\n\n$ bun run format:check\n$ prettier --check .\nChecking formatting...\nAll matched files use Prettier code style!\n```\nBoth clean.\n\n### git status before commit (confirms scope)\n\n```\nChanges to be committed:\n\tmodified:   packages/extension-chrome/e2e/a4-evidence.spec.ts\n\tmodified:   packages/extension-chrome/e2e/keyboard-commands.spec.ts\n\tmodified:   packages/extension-chrome/e2e/lookup-pending-dismiss.spec.ts\n```\nOnly the three named spec files staged; nothing else modified in the working tree.\n\n### Commit\n\n```\ngit commit -m \"test: open onboarding on install — target the page under test in command-relay e2e so the install tab does not steal the command (C1)\" -m $'Tribe-Card: c1-open-on-install\\nTribe-Task: 3b/3'\n```\nCommit SHA: `da5e236` (`3 files changed, 8 insertions(+)`).\n\nPer this task's brief (fix-scope, exact `git add` list of the three spec files given explicitly),\nthe plan file's checkboxes were not touched — consistent with Task 3's precedent recorded above in\nthis same report file.\nEOF\necho done"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"s