{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JvrSNNki2iDofk1c5LNjMD","type":"tool_result","content":"614\t#### C1 — Open onboarding on install `Impact 5 · Effort S · Score 5.0` · **foundation**\n615\t\n616\t- **Today:** Installing the extension does nothing — `sw.ts` has no `chrome.runtime.onInstalled`\n617\t  listener. The welcome screen (`onboarding-view`, options page) is only ever reached if the user\n618\t  happens to select text, spot the ~20px Define button, click it, get the no-key card, and click\n619\t  \"Open Settings\" — or finds the side panel via the toolbar icon.\n620\t- **Missing:** On `onInstalled` with `reason === 'install'`, open `options.html` once so the very\n621\t  first thing a new user sees is the welcome screen.\n622\t- **Why:** The drop happens before the product's first screen is ever seen; an onboarding page that\n623\t  nobody reaches cannot onboard anybody.\n624\t- **Payoff:** 100% of new installs see Welcome → key setup, instead of the lucky few.\n625\t- **Scope fence:** Fires **only** on `reason === 'install'` (never on `'update'`); opens exactly one\n626\t  tab, once — no re-prompting loop; skipped entirely when the build bakes an env key. No new\n627\t  permission (`runtime.onInstalled` needs none).\n628\t- **Depends on:** — · **Lead decides:** nothing else; this is deliberately minimal. **Escalate:** none.\n629\t- **Landing-page note (2026-07-16):** the install target stays the extension's OWN welcome screen,\n630\t  not the landing page — key entry must stay inside the extension (S1: the website never touches\n631\t  the key), and the welcome screen works offline. The welcome screen may link to the landing page\n632\t  as \"the full guide\"; the funnel's try-it step moves there only after activation (C3).\n633\t\n634\t#### C2 — Verified activation `Impact 5 · Effort S · Score 5.0` · **foundation**\n635\t\n636\t- **Today:** \"Save & activate\" accepts any non-empty string — `onboarding-view.submit()` checks only\n637\t  `length > 0`, `options.ts` persists it and immediately shows **\"You're all set.\"** The wire\n638\t  message `connection.test` and its router path already exist but are reachable only from the\n639\t  settings form. A wrong/expired key therefore fails **later**, as a red \"Lookup failed\" card in\n640\t  the middle of reading.\n641\t- **Missing:** Activation runs one real, user-triggered `connection.test` round-trip with the pasted\n642\t  key and only claims success when the provider answers; failures render inline with actionable\n643\t  copy (typo? expired? quota?).\n644\t- **Why:** A false \"all set\" converts a setup error into product distrust — the user believes the\n645\t  extension is broken, not the key.\n646\t- **Payoff:** Bad keys are caught at paste time, in the one place the user is already looking.\n647\t- **Scope fence:** Exactly one test call per explicit \"Save & activate\" click (constraint 4 holds:\n648\t  user-triggered, and the cost is ~one token). Timeout + offline get their own copy. Reuses the\n649\t  existing `connection.test` path — no new wire message unless the key-under-test can't ride it.\n650\t- **Depends on:** — · **Lead decides:** persist-on-pass vs. persist-with-warning semantics (recommend\n651\t  persist only on pass, with a \"save anyway\" escape hatch for offline setups). **Escalate:** none.\n652\t\n653\t#### C8 — Gesture demo on the welcome screen `Impact 4 · Effort S · Score 4.0`\n654\t\n655\t- **Today:** The welcome lead paragraph _tells_ (\"Look up any English word right where you're\n656\t  reading\") but never _shows_ the select → Define gesture; after activation the settings status\n657\t  line again tells (\"Highlight any word…\") with nothing to practice on.\n658\t- **Missing:** A small inline demo on the onboarding surface itself — a real sentence with a word\n659\t  that visibly gets selected and sprouts the Define pill (CSS/inline-SVG animation, token-themed),\n660\t  so the gesture is understood before the user ever leaves setup.\n661\t- **Why:** The product's trigger is an invisible gesture; users who never learn it churn with a\n662\t  correctly configured key.\n663\t- **Payoff:** Every user leaves onboarding knowing exactly what motion produces a definition.\n664\t- **Scope fence:** Pure UI demo — **0 API calls**, no video assets, `--ad-*`/`--adp-*` tokens only,\n665\t  honors reduced-motion. Works before a key exists.\n666\t- **Depends on:** — (pairs naturally with C3) · **Lead decides:** demo copy/animation. **Escalate:** none.\n667\t- **Landing-page note (2026-07-16):** the landing page's hero already renders a static demo card\n668\t  (`docs/index.html`); the animated gesture snippet built here should be authored so the page can\n669\t  reuse it (same tokens both sides). The on-welcome demo stays — it must work offline and before\n670\t  any tab switch — but \"see it in action\" may link to the landing demo.\n671\t\n672\t#### C5 — Key paste hygiene & format hints `Impact 3 · Effort S · Score 3.0`\n673\t\n674\t- **Today:** The key input saves verbatim. A trailing newline from a copy, smart quotes from a chat\n675\t  app, or an OpenAI `sk-…` key pasted into the Gemini-only field are all accepted silently and fail\n676\t  later as INVALID_KEY. The placeholder \"AIza…\" is the only format guidance.\n677\t- **Missing:** Trim whitespace/quotes on paste; recognize known prefixes (`AIza` Gemini · `sk-ant-`\n678\t  Anthropic · `sk-` OpenAI) and hint when the key looks like a different provider's; flag obviously\n679\t  malformed input inline before activation.\n680\t- **Why:** Key-paste errors are invisible typos — the user did everything right and still fails,\n681\t  with no clue why.\n682\t- **Payoff:** The most common activation failure class disappears before the test call even runs.\n683\t- **Scope fence:** Heuristic **hints**, never hard blocks (providers change formats); the key never\n684\t  appears in any log or message (S1); pure client-side string checks.\n685\t- **Depends on:** — · **Lead decides:** hint copy, prefix table. **Escalate:** none.\n686\t\n687\t#### C6 — Invalid-key recovery flow `Impact 3 · Effort S · Score 3.0`\n688\t\n689\t- **Today:** A rejected key renders \"Lookup failed / Google rejected the API key.\" with an \"Open\n690\t  Settings\" button that lands on the generic settings form — key field unfocused, no explanation of\n691\t  causes, no retest; the user re-enters a key blind and must find \"Test connection\" themselves.\n692\t- **Missing:** The INVALID_KEY card deep-links to the options page in a fix-key mode (key row\n693\t  focused, likely causes listed, connection test auto-run after the edit) — the same landing the"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01B9iSw7CJVDP18fuoGDhi4c","session_id":"1582a562-7cd7-4915-90db-f6e0a641a53f","uuid":"e885e6e1-50f8-4f41-bceb-235e9174e1b7","timestamp":"2026-07-24T00:16:45.621Z","subagent_type":"tribe:skinner","task_description":"Skinner: audit C1 done-ness"}
