 done. Not yet at the \"PR opened\" stage — no blocking code defects, but review one Important finding (flaky e2e timing) before treating the card as shipped.\n\nRelevant paths: `/Users/todd.lam/WORK/_TestScripts/ai-dict/.claude/worktrees/c1-open-on-install/packages/extension-chrome/src/sw.ts`, `/Users/todd.lam/WORK/_TestScripts/ai-dict/.claude/worktrees/c1-open-on-install/packages/extension-chrome/e2e/c1-open-on-install.spec.ts`, `/Users/todd.lam/WORK/_TestScripts/ai-dict/.claude/worktrees/c1-open-on-install/packages/app/src/domain/onboarding-policy.ts`, `/Users/todd.lam/WORK/_TestScripts/ai-dict/.claude/worktrees/c1-open-on-install/docs/tribe/campaigns/least-effort-5/answers.md`, `/Users/todd.lam/WORK/_TestScripts/ai-dict/.claude/state/least-effort-5/reports/C1.md`."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: acac5144251935031 (use SendMessage with to: 'acac5144251935031', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent)\n<usage>subagent_tokens: 134478\ntool_uses: 54\nduration_ms: 1055005</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1582a562-7cd7-4915-90db-f6e0a641a53f","uuid":"92e404f2-bfb6-40ab-af2d-ed699b74bed0","timestamp":"2026-07-24T00:29:13.359Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Adversarially audit whether campaign card C1 is ACTUALLY done on branch\n`feature/C1OpenOnInstallLE5` in worktree\n`/Users/todd.lam/WORK/_TestScripts/ai-dict/.claude/worktrees/c1-open-on-install`.\nVerify by RUNNING proofs, not by trusting claims. Read-only — do not edit or commit.\n\n## Requirement contract (in priority order)\n1. Spec: `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-16-c1-open-on-install-design.md`\n2. Plan: `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-16-c1-open-on-install.md`\n3. Binding campaign rulings that SUPERSEDE parts of the plan (this is critical — verify against\n   these, not the superseded plan text):\n   - **R1**: the listener must NOT use `chrome.runtime.openOptionsPage()` at install (it creates no\n     tab at cold launch). It must use `chrome.tabs.create({ url: chrome.runtime.getURL('options.html') })`.\n     No new manifest permission (no `chrome.tabs.query`, no `tabs` permission).\n   - **R3**: because the install tab lingers, pre-existing e2e tests that click a control calling\n     `openOptionsPage()` and wait for a NEW page must be adapted in-arrange (close the install tab)\n     while KEEPING a falsifiable assertion; the router/product must NOT change.\n\n## C1 scope fence — verify each holds\n- Fires ONLY on `reason === 'install'`, never `'update'` (and not chrome_update/shared_module_update).\n- Skipped entirely when the build baked an env key (`ENV_API_KEY`).\n- Opens exactly one tab, once — no re-prompting loop, no persisted \"already shown\" flag.\n- No new manifest permission (`manifest.json` permissions stay `[\"storage\",\"sidePanel\"]`;\n  `manifest.test.ts` unchanged & green).\n- Domain purity: `packages/app/src/domain/onboarding-policy.ts` has NO chrome.* import; `reason`\n  typed `string`.\n\n## What to verify by running (foreground, timeout 600000 on heavy commands)\n- `git log --oneline origin/master..HEAD` and `git diff origin/master..HEAD` — confirm the change is\n  what's claimed and additive; confirm `sw.ts` uses `chrome.tabs.create`, not `openOptionsPage`, in\n  the onInstalled listener; confirm the decision is delegated to `shouldOpenOnboardingOnInstall`.\n- Unit: `cd packages/app && bunx vitest run test/onboarding-policy.test.ts` (4-branch coverage +\n  other reasons) and the full `bun run test`.\n- Typecheck both packages; `bun run lint`; `bun run format:check`.\n- e2e (build CI-style first — this shell exports GEMINI_API_KEY): \n  `env -u GEMINI_API_KEY GA4_MEASUREMENT_ID=G-E2ETEST GA4_API_SECRET=e2e-secret bun run build:chrome`\n  then `cd packages/extension-chrome && bunx playwright test c1-open-on-install.spec.ts onboarding.spec.ts settings-nav.spec.ts side-panel.spec.ts keyboard-commands.spec.ts lookup-pending-dismiss.spec.ts c10-funnel.spec.ts --reporter=list`.\n- Confirm the new e2e assertion is falsifiable, not tautological (the c1 spec asserts onboarding-view\n  + #key on the install-opened tab; check it would fail if no tab opened).\n\n## Adversarial angles to probe (self-refute before reporting)\n- Does the onInstalled listener truly gate on the domain predicate, or could it open a tab on\n  'update'? Trace the code.\n- Could `ENV_API_KEY` being set fail to skip? (`Boolean(ENV_API_KEY)` passed as envKeyBaked.)\n- Did any change sneak into `manifest.json`, the router, `wire.ts`, `helpers.ts`, or safari?\n- Is the R3 onboarding-test fix genuinely falsifiable or was a live assertion silently gutted?\n- Any hidden e2e regression from the install tab beyond what was fixed? (You may run the full suite\n  if you want: `bunx playwright test` — but note 17 evidence/store specs are env-gated skips and\n  `error-reporting:143` GA4 assertion only passes with the dummy GA4 build creds above.)\n\nReport a severity-ranked findings list with a conformance matrix (each contract item →\nPASS/FAIL + evidence). Every finding must survive self-refutation. Write your full report to\n`/Users/todd.lam/WORK/_TestScripts/ai-dict/.claude/state/least-effort-5/reports/C1.md`\n(append \"## Skinner audit — C1\"), and give me a concise verdict summary (is it done? blocking issues?).","agentId":"acac5144251935031","agentType":"tribe:skinner","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I was instructed to write this report to `/Users/todd.lam/WORK/_TestScripts/ai-dict/.claude/state/least-effort-5/reports/C1.md`, but per my standing tool instructions I do not write report/analysis files — I only have Read/Bash/Skill tools and no file-write capability was extended to me for this purpose. The full report is below for the caller to persist if needed.\n\n## Skinner audit — C1\n\n### Source of truth\n- Contract level: caller-given (spec + plan + explicit campaign rulings R1/R3, cross-checked against the committed `docs/tribe/campaigns/least-effort-5/answers.md` — confirmed genuine, not fabricated in the dispatch)\n- Spec: `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-16-c1-open-on-install-design.md` / Plan: `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-16-c1-open-on-install.md` / Rulings: `docs/tribe/campaigns/least-effort-5/answers.md` R1 (lines 39-77), R3 (lines 106-153)\n- Governance loaded: root `CLAUDE.md`, worktree `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/rules/workflow-conventions.md`, `.claude/rules/test-first.md`, `.c3/` markdown (CLI unavailable, read directly), `rule-domain-purity`/`ref-core-dependency-rule`\n\n### Conformance matrix\n| # | Requirement | Source | Satisfied? | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Listener must NOT use `openOptionsPage()`; must use `chrome.tabs.create({url: chrome.runtime.getURL('options.html')})` | R1 | ✅ | `packages/extension-chrome/src/sw.ts:206-215` |\n| 2 | No `chrome.tabs.query`, no new manifest permission | R1 | ✅ | `grep chrome.tabs.query` → 0 hits; `manifest.json` permissions still `[\"storage\",\"sidePanel\"]`; `manifest.test.ts` 6/6 pass |\n| 3 | Pre-existing tests adapted in-arrange (close install tab), assertion stays falsifiable, router/product unchanged | R3 | ✅ | `onboarding.spec.ts`, `settings-nav.spec.ts`, `side-panel.spec.ts` diffs — only a close-tab loop inserted before unchanged `waitForEvent('page')`; `router.ts`/`wire.ts` diff empty |\n| 4 | Fires only on `reason==='install'`, never `update`/`chrome_update`/`shared_module_update` | Scope fence | ✅ | `onboarding-policy.ts:13`; 5 unit tests incl. the two extra-reason cases, all green |\n| 5 | Skipped when build baked `ENV_API_KEY` | Scope fence | ✅ | `Boolean(ENV_API_KEY)` passed at `sw.ts`; unit test `('install', true) → false` |\n| 6 | Exactly one tab, once, no persisted flag | Scope fence | ✅ | no `chrome.storage` read/write added; e2e asserts exactly 1 tab (22/22 pass in required run) |\n| 7 | No new manifest permission | Scope fence | ✅ | see #2 |\n| 8 | `onboarding-policy.ts` chrome-free, `reason: string` | Domain purity | ✅ | file has zero `import` statements; `bun run lint`'s dep-direction check passed |\n| 9 | Full unit suite green | Plan | ✅ | `bun run test` → 695/695 passed |\n| 10 | Typecheck both packages | Plan | ✅ | `tsc --noEmit` clean, both packages |\n| 11 | Lint / format clean | Plan | ✅ | both clean |\n| 12 | Required e2e set (7 files) green | Task brief | ✅ | 22/22 passed, one run |\n| 13 | New e2e assertion falsifiable, not tautological | R3 mandatory guard | ✅ | unchanged `waitForEvent('page')` (would time out if CTA broken); corroborated by Hunter's own RED/GREEN transcript in `.claude/state/least-effort-5/reports/C1.md` (not independently re-run by me — reproducing it requires mutating `sw.ts`, which the contract-lens mutation ban forbids) |\n| 14 | `packages/extension-safari` untouched | Decision 2.4 | ✅ | `git diff --stat -- packages/extension-safari/` empty |\n| 15 | No hidden e2e regression beyond what was fixed | Adversarial probe | ⚠️ | see Findings — one reproducible flake found in the new C1 spec itself under full-suite load |\n| 16 | No governance tripwires (Co-authored-by, raw.githubusercontent, hand-edited `.c3`, direct-to-master) | Step 6 | ✅ | commit log clean, branch is not master |\n\n### Proof run\n- `cd packages/app && bunx vitest run test/onboarding-policy.test.ts` → PASS — 5 tests, 5 passed\n- `bun run test` (full repo) → PASS — 54 files, 695 tests\n- `cd packages/app && bun run typecheck` → PASS — clean\n- `cd packages/extension-chrome && bun run typecheck` → PASS — clean\n- `bun run lint` → PASS\n- `bun run format:check` → PASS\n- `cd packages/extension-chrome && bunx vitest run test/manifest.test.ts` → PASS — 6/6, confirms no permission crept in\n- `env -u GEMINI_API_KEY GA4_MEASUREMENT_ID=... bun run build:chrome` → PASS\n- `bunx playwright test c1-open-on-install.spec.ts onboarding.spec.ts settings-nav.spec.ts side-panel.spec.ts keyboard-commands.spec.ts lookup-pending-dismiss.spec.ts c10-funnel.spec.ts --reporter=list` → PASS — 22/22\n- `bunx playwright test --reporter=list` (full suite, exploratory) → **FAIL** — 117 passed, 1 failed (`c1-open-on-install.spec.ts`), 17 skipped (env-gated, expected)\n- Repro attempts on the failing scenario (19-test prefix isolated, ×2 repeat-each=2, c1 spec alone ×5) → all PASS — confirms a low-frequency, load-correlated flake, not a deterministic defect\n\n### Findings\n\n#### Critical — breaks conformance\nNone found.\n\n#### Important\n- **[`packages/extension-chrome/e2e/c1-open-on-install.spec.ts:14-17`] The new C1 e2e assertion is flaky under sustained system load.** In a full-suite run (`bunx playwright test`, 135 tests, single worker, 6.5 min), the C1 spec failed with `Expected: 1, Received: 0` after its 10-second `.poll()` timeout — the install-opened options tab hadn't materialized in time. Isolated reruns of the identical 19-test prefix (twice) and the spec alone (×5) all passed, pointing to load-correlated timing rather than a logic defect: the `chrome.runtime.onInstalled` → `chrome.tabs.create` mechanism itself is correct (proven by the 5/5 domain unit tests and every other clean run), but the test's fixed 10s poll window is tight relative to the config's own 60s global test timeout and to the acknowledged risk class the suite's own `playwright.config.ts` comment names (\"several in parallel... starves CPU/display and causes... timeouts\"). CI's `retries: process.env.CI ? 1 : 0` masks this in the real pipeline, but a local `bunx playwright test` (no `CI` env) — exactly the workflow-conventions.md-mandated way to drive this suite — would intermittently fail on this spec with no code regression. Evidence: full-suite output lines 22 and 141-169 (`Timeout 10000ms exceeded... Received: 0`), followed by 3 clean reproductions of the same ordering (36s, 1.2m×2 runs) and 5/5 in isolation.\n\n#### Minor / nits\n- R3 states a preference order (assert tab-focus transition first; fall back to close-and-reuse only \"if activation cannot be observed reliably\"). The Hunter's report goes straight to the fallback without documenting why option 1 was infeasible. Not a functional defect — the mandatory falsifiability guard was independently satisfied and proven (RED/GREEN transcript in `C1.md`) — but a minor process-rigor gap against the letter of R3.\n- No PR has been opened yet for `feature/C1OpenOnInstallLE5` (`gh pr list` returns none). R3's closing mandate — that the PR's \"Testing performed\" section must explicitly say the plan's \"no existing test's assertions change\" claim is superseded — cannot yet be checked because no PR body exists. Not a code defect; simply not yet reached in the workflow.\n- Plan-file checkboxes (`docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-16-c1-open-on-install.md`) remain unticked across all 3(+3b) commits, per the Hunter's own explicit note that this was deferred to the Warchief. Tracking-only, no functional impact.\n\n### Unverified claims\n- The Hunter's report (`C1.md`) documents a RED→GREEN falsifiability proof for the R3 guard (temporarily breaking `sw.ts`'s `openOptions` callback, rebuilding, observing a timeout, restoring, observing green). I did not independently reproduce this because doing so requires mutating tracked source, which the contract-lens mutation ban forbids me from doing even temporarily. I instead verified the weaker-but-sufficient claim myself: the assertion code (`waitForEvent('page')`) is unchanged from the pre-existing test and is structurally falsifiable by inspection, and the current suite passes end-to-end.\n\n### Scope creep\nNone found — every changed file traces to a spec/plan/ruling requirement (domain predicate + export, `sw.ts` listener, new C1 e2e spec, the 4 R3 arrange-fixes, the 3 R3-adjacent command-relay `bringToFront()` fixes for the same install-tab side effect).\n\n### Refuted during self-audit\n- Initially suspected the full-suite e2e failure indicated a real bug in the `onInstalled` → `chrome.tabs.create` mechanism itself. Refuted: 5 unit-test branches pass, the required-proof e2e run passes cleanly, and the same failing test/order combination passed on 4 further attempts (isolated and at 2x/5x repeat) — the mechanism is correct; only the specific poll timeout is marginal under sustained load, which downgrades this from a functional bug to a test-robustness issue (kept as Important, not Critical, given CI's existing retry mitigates it in practice).\n\nCONTRACT-LENS: 1 findings — 1 important (0 critical, 3 minor/nits not counted toward tally)\n\n---\n\n**Concise verdict summary:** C1's implementation is functionally complete and correctly conforms to the spec, plan, and both superseding campaign rulings (R1's `chrome.tabs.create` mechanism swap, R3's test-arrange fix) — every unit test, typecheck, lint, format, and the exact required e2e proof set (22/22) pass cleanly, domain purity and the no-new-permission fence both hold, and Safari/router/wire/manifest are all correctly untouched. The one real issue found is that the new `c1-open-on-install.spec.ts` e2e test is flaky under sustained load (reproduced once in 6 attempts, only after ~6+ minutes of prior test-suite load) — a real but non-blocking robustness gap in the test's 10-second poll window, mitigated by CI's existing retry policy but worth tightening before calling this fully done. Not yet at the \"PR opened\" stage — no blocking code defects, but review one Important finding (flaky e2e timing) before treating the card as shipped.\n\nRelevant paths: `/Users/todd.lam/WORK/_TestScripts/ai-dict/.claude/worktrees/c1-open-on-install/packages/extension-chrome/src/sw.ts`, `/Users/todd.lam/WORK/_TestScripts/ai-dict/.claude/worktrees/c1-open-on-install/packages/extension-chrome/e2e/c1-open-on-install.spec.ts`, `/Users/todd.lam/WORK/_TestScripts/ai-dict/.claude/worktrees/c1-open-on-install/packages/app/src/domain/onboarding-policy.ts`, `/Users/todd.lam/WORK/_TestScripts/ai-dict/.claude/worktrees/c1-open-on-install/docs/tribe/campaigns/least-effort-5/answers.md`, `/Users/todd.lam/WORK/_TestScripts/ai-dict/.claude/state/least-effort-5/reports/C1.md`."}],"resolvedModel":"claude-sonnet-5","totalDurationMs":1055005,"totalTokens":134478,"totalToolUseCount":54,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4300,"cache_read_input_tokens":125590,"output_tokens":4586,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4300},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4586,"cache_read_input_tokens":125590,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4300,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4300,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":6,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":48,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
