{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdKwxgcZCCWLEZVxqURaS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KSZ9euiDuEpKcSqTH2PUg2","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/todd.lam/WORK/_TestScripts/ai-dict/.claude/worktrees/c1-open-on-install\ncat > /tmp/c1-pr-body.md <<'EOF'\n## Description\nA fresh extension install now opens `options.html`'s welcome screen (`<onboarding-view>`) automatically, so every new install reaches Welcome → key setup instead of only the few who stumble into it via the no-key card or side panel. A new pure domain predicate `shouldOpenOnboardingOnInstall(reason, envKeyBaked)` decides; a `chrome.runtime.onInstalled` listener in `sw.ts` acts on it. Fires only on `reason === 'install'`, skips env-key builds, opens one tab once — **no product/router/manifest change; the only new source is the domain predicate + the sw.ts listener.**\n\n## Design choices\n- Uses `chrome.tabs.create({ url: chrome.runtime.getURL('options.html') })` at install, not `chrome.runtime.openOptionsPage()` (ruling R1: `openOptionsPage()` at cold `--load-extension` launch resolves without creating a tab). Needs no new manifest permission — `permissions` stays `[\"storage\",\"sidePanel\"]`.\n- The install tab lingers in the e2e fixture's per-test fresh profile, so pre-existing tests that reach the options page were adapted **in-arrange only** (ruling R3): 4 `waitForEvent('page')` tests (`onboarding`, `settings-nav` ×2, `side-panel`) close the install tab first; 3 `relayCommand` specs (`keyboard-commands`, `lookup-pending-dismiss`, `a4-evidence`) bring the page-under-test to front so the SW command relay targets it. Assertions stay falsifiable; router/product untouched.\n- The plan's §5.5 claim \"no existing test's assertions change\" is **superseded** — it rested on `openOptionsPage()` creating no tab, which R1 disproved.\n\n## Testing performed\n- `bun run test` — 695/695 unit tests pass (54 files), incl. 5 new `onboarding-policy.test.ts` branch tests (`install`/`update`/`chrome_update`/`shared_module_update` × env-key) and the untouched `manifest.test.ts` permission guard (6/6, proves no permission crept in).\n- `tsc --noEmit` clean on `@ai-dict/app` and `@ai-dict/extension-chrome`; `bun run lint` (dep-direction inward + eslint) and `bun run format:check` clean.\n- Full Playwright e2e (CI-equivalent build, `GEMINI_API_KEY` cleared + dummy GA4 creds): **118 passed, 0 failed, 17 skipped** (env-gated evidence/store specs). New `c1-open-on-install.spec.ts` asserts a fresh install opens exactly one `options.html` tab showing `<onboarding-view>` with the key field.\n- R3 falsifiability proof recorded: temporarily breaking the CTA turned the `onboarding.spec.ts` reuse test RED (`waitForEvent('page')` timeout), restoring turned it GREEN.\n- Command-relay determinism verified with `--repeat-each=3` (21/21) and the C1 poll-window hardening with `--repeat-each=5` (5/5) to remove a load-correlated flake the Skinner found.\n\n## Scope fence held\nFires only on `install` (never `update`); skipped when the build bakes an env key; one tab once (Chrome's single-fire `onInstalled` is the whole no-reprompt guarantee — no persisted flag); no new manifest permission; `packages/app/src/domain/onboarding-policy.ts` stays chrome-free (`reason: string`); Safari shell / router / wire / manifest untouched.\nEOF\ngh pr create --base master --head feature/C1OpenOnInstallLE5 \\\n  --title \"feat: open onboarding on install (C1)\" \\\n  --body-file /tmp/c1-pr-body.md 2>&1 | tail -5","description":"Open the C1 PR"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":781,"cache_read_input_tokens":174457,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":781},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1582a562-7cd7-4915-90db-f6e0a641a53f","uuid":"627f284d-c6fd-443c-a363-17a3734ad28e","timestamp":"2026-07-24T00:38:28.814Z","request_id":"req_011CdKwxfV6N9Ft3DfYucMhY"}
